58% to 45%-47% (having bottomed at 40%-43%). Management frames this as temporary caution in a \"cautionary environment\" (Middle East war, LPG shortage, uneven monsoon), not a demand problem, and holds the Rs. 30,000 crore-by-2030 AUM goal on 27%-28% CAGR. Spread discipline (>6%) and a 2x-regulatory ECL buffer are the trade-off for the slower top line.","trig":[]},"lm":"","m":7278,"mem":0,"pdd":"","prev_stage":1,"prev_zone_vpe":null,"r":null,"s":"INDIASHLTR","sig":"","sx":{"SMA_50":"754.0","base_count":"","drawdown_from_prev_signal":"","duration_from_prev_signal":"","pct_below_52w_high":"31.0","pct_change_from_prev_signal":"","pivot_close":"","pivot_low":"","stage_changed_since_prev_signal":"","vpe_df_60d_sum":"-0.5","vpe_zone_cumul_df":""},"t":""}},"s":"INDIASHLTR"}